<p style="font-size: 1.04rem; line-height: 1.75; color: #f1f5f9; font-weight: 500; margin-bottom: 12px;"><strong>Daylight condition re‑inspection</strong> is performed under natural light to eliminate shadows or artificial lighting that could hide imperfections.</p>
<ul style="list-style: none; padding-left: 0; margin: 16px 0 20px 0; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 10px;"><li style="display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px; background: rgba(255,255,255,0.03); border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.07); padding: 10px 14px; border-radius: 8px; font-size: 0.92rem; line-height: 1.55; color: #cbd5e1;"><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; margin-top: 4px; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: 0.9rem;"></i><span>The receiver compares the vehicle’s current exterior and interior with the high‑resolution pickup photographs, checking for new scratches, dents, paint chips, or missing accessories.</span></li><li style="display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px; background: rgba(255,255,255,0.03); border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.07); padding: 10px 14px; border-radius: 8px; font-size: 0.92rem; line-height: 1.55; color: #cbd5e1;"><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; margin-top: 4px; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: 0.9rem;"></i><span>Any discrepancy is photographed, noted, and discussed on the spot, ensuring an accurate visual record before the vehicle is accepted.</span></li></ul>

<p><strong>Odometer verification against the LR bilty</strong> involves reading the odometer and matching it to the mileage recorded on the logistics receipt (LR bilty). This step confirms that the vehicle has not been driven beyond the agreed distance, which could affect warranty or lease terms.</p>
<p>The verifier writes the current reading on the bilty, signs next to it, and captures a close‑up photo of the odometer display for audit purposes.</p>

<p style="font-size: 1.04rem; line-height: 1.75; color: #f1f5f9; font-weight: 500; margin-bottom: 12px;"><strong>Signed condition sign‑off</strong> finalizes the handover.</p>
<ul style="list-style: none; padding-left: 0; margin: 16px 0 20px 0; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 10px;"><li style="display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px; background: rgba(255,255,255,0.03); border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.07); padding: 10px 14px; border-radius: 8px; font-size: 0.92rem; line-height: 1.55; color: #cbd5e1;"><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; margin-top: 4px; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: 0.9rem;"></i><span>After the visual and mileage checks, the recipient signs a condition report that references the pickup photos, the verified odometer reading, and any noted discrepancies.</span></li><li style="display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px; background: rgba(255,255,255,0.03); border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.07); padding: 10px 14px; border-radius: 8px; font-size: 0.92rem; line-height: 1.55; color: #cbd5e1;"><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; margin-top: 4px; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: 0.9rem;"></i><span>The sign‑off includes the date, time, and names of both parties, creating a legally binding acknowledgment that the vehicle was received in the documented state.</span></li></ul>

<h3>Key Benefits</h3>
<ul>
<li>Provides a transparent, evidence‑based record that protects both sender and receiver from disputes.</li>
<li>Ensures compliance with contractual mileage limits and warranty conditions.</li>
<li>Creates a clear audit trail for insurance, regulatory, and internal quality‑control reviews.</li>
</ul>

<p>By adhering to this three‑step handover—daylight re‑inspection, odometer verification, and signed sign‑off—logistics teams can deliver two‑wheelers and motorcycles with confidence, minimizing risk and maintaining trust throughout the supply chain.</p></div>
